{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.QBetaProxyHReduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.QBetaProxyHReduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QBetaProxyHReduction.qbeta_proxy_over_h_eq_E0_reduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QBetaProxyHReduction.qbeta_proxy_over_h_eq_E0_reduction","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QBetaProxyHReduction.lean#L56-L62","doc":"**Scale form.** Dividing by the bandwidth `h ≠ 0`: the `1/h`-scale is\n`E₀·(2−h)/2 = E₀·(1 − h/2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QBetaProxyHReduction.qbeta_proxy_eq_E0_h_reduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QBetaProxyHReduction.qbeta_proxy_eq_E0_h_reduction","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QBetaProxyHReduction.lean#L46-L54","doc":"**Exact reduction.** The CAL-2 proxy `Q_β` equals the categorical scale\n`E₀` times the smoothed bar-average `h·(2−h)/2` of the single interface\ncrossing — an algebraic identity in the fraction field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QBetaProxyHReduction.QbetaProxy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QBetaProxyHReduction.QbetaProxy","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QBetaProxyHReduction.lean#L42-L44","doc":"The CAL-2 proxy `Q_β` closed form (numerator resolved on the substrate\nbranch `1 < q < 1+√2`, where `|q²−2q−1| = 2q − q² + 1`), in `m_e` units. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QBetaProxyHReduction.E0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QBetaProxyHReduction.E0","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QBetaProxyHReduction.lean#L39-L40","doc":"The categorical scale `E₀ = 1/(q(q−1))` (in `m_e` units). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QBetaProxyHReduction.hOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QBetaProxyHReduction.hOf","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QBetaProxyHReduction.lean#L36-L37","doc":"The bandwidth `h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}